This is a festive article for Halloween, which falls in heading 9505. Subheading 9505.10 covers Christmas articles, and 9505.90 covers other festive articles, including Halloween. The 9505.90 split is 9505.90.2000 for "Artificial Christmas trees" and 9505.90.4000 for "Other: Festive, carnival or other entertainment articles"? Looking at the current HTSUS: 9505.10 is Articles for Christmas festivities. 9505.90 is Other, with 9505.90.20 for Confetti, paper spirals or tinsel; 9505.90.40 for Magic tricks and practical joke articles; 9505.90.60 for Other.

The material is likely plastic or resin, but 9505 is not classified by material, so 9505.90.6000 applies.

